msgid "Migration Guide"
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"As usual, this new Quarkus version comes with some exciting new features\n"
"but we put the focus this month on fixing issues and improving things all "
"over the place, documentation included."
msgstr ""

msgid "Quarkus 1.7, that's more than 300 pull requests merged."
msgstr ""

msgid "The most prominent new features are:"
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"New extensions for the low level and high level Elasticsearch REST clients"
msgstr ""

msgid "An extension for the Vert.x Redis client"
msgstr ""

msgid "An Hibernate Envers extension"
msgstr ""

msgid "Support for the JDBC Db2 driver"
msgstr ""

msgid "A lot of improvements to the Reactive routes feature"
msgstr ""

msgid "The Funqy serverless framework got some interesting new features"
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"We also reworked link:/guides/[our Guides index page] recently with a new "
"design and a search engine."
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"Eager to migrate your existing applications? Here is https://github.com/"
"quarkusio/quarkus/wiki/Migration-Guide-1.7[our migration guide for 1.7]."
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"One important point is that we don't support GraalVM 19.3 anymore:\n"
"GraalVM 20.1 in its Java 11 flavor is the recommended GraalVM version."
msgstr ""

msgid "What&#8217;s new?"
msgstr ""

msgid "Elasticsearch REST Clients"
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"Quarkus has support for the low level Elasticsearch REST client for a while "
"but it wasn't publicly exposed.\n"
"It was just used under the hoods by the Hibernate Search + Elasticsearch "
"extension."
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"In 1.7, both the low level and high level Elasticsearch REST clients are "
"exposed via extensions with proper Quarkus configuration.\n"
"Thus you can connect to your Elasticsearch clusters directly."
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"More information about how to use these clients can be found in link:/guides/"
"elasticsearch[the new Elasticsearch guide]."
msgstr ""

msgid "Vert.x Redis Client"
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"Quarkus 1.7 introduces a new extension to connect to the Redis datastore.\n"
"It is based on the Eclipse Vert.x Redis client."
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"Everything you need to know about it is in link:/guides/redis[the Redis "
"guide]."
msgstr ""

msgid "Hibernate Envers"
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"Hibernate Envers is an Hibernate ORM module bringing versioning/auditing "
"features."
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"It used to work with Quarkus in JVM mode but not in native mode.\n"
"The new Hibernate Envers extension fixes that."
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"You can find more information about it in link:/guides/hibernate-"
"orm#envers[the Hibernate Envers section] of the Hibernate ORM guide."
msgstr ""

msgid "Funqy Improvements"
msgstr ""

msgid "Funqy is our serverless framework."
msgstr ""

msgid "Two new features were added to Funqy in 1.7:"
msgstr ""

msgid "The ability to inject query parameters in the Funqy HTTP bindings"
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"The support for link:/guides/funqy-gcp-functions[Google Cloud Platform]"
msgstr ""

msgid "Reactive Routes Improvements"
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"While most Quarkus applications are developed with RESTEasy and JAX-RS,\n"
"you can go with an alternative approach called link:/guides/reactive-"
"routes[Reactive Routes]\n"
"where you declare and chain routes."
msgstr ""

msgid "Reactive Routes got several improvements in 1.7:"
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"The `@Param`, `@Header` and `@Body` annotations were added to inject "
"elements from the request in the route handling method."
msgstr ""

msgid "Mutiny types are now fully supported."
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"If the route handling method doesn't return `void`, you can now simplify "
"things by not passing the `RoutingExchange` as a parameter."
msgstr ""

msgid "Db2 JDBC driver"
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"In 1.6, we included support for the reactive Db2 driver.\n"
"1.7 brings a new extension for the Db2 JDBC driver."
msgstr ""

msgid "Security Testing Infrastructure"
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"When testing, it might be handy to disable security entirely or use a "
"particular identity."
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"Quarkus 1.7 introduces the `@TestSecurity` annotation which allows all that, "
"as explained in link:/guides/security-testing#testing-security[the Security "
"Testing guide]."
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"In passing the whole Security documentation got a massive reorganization to "
"make it more approachable."
msgstr ""

msgid "Extension Registry"
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"This feature paves the way for the future:\n"
"we now support multiple extension registries,\n"
"meaning you could host your own extension registry and get it integrated in "
"the Quarkus tools."
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"We are still making progress on this front but expect to see some real use "
"cases for it soon."
msgstr ""

msgid "S2I image"
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"The default S2I image is now a Java 11 image based on UBI: `registry.access."
"redhat.com/ubi8/openjdk-11`."
msgstr ""

msgid "Full Changelog"
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"You can get the full changelogs of https://github.com/quarkusio/quarkus/"
"releases/tag/1.7.0.CR1[1.7.0.CR1] and https://github.com/quarkusio/quarkus/"
"releases/tag/1.7.0.Final[1.7.0.Final] on GitHub."
msgstr ""

msgid "ADOPTERS.md"
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"To share stories about Quarkus usage, we added https://github.com/quarkusio/"
"quarkus/blob/master/ADOPTERS.md[an `ADOPTERS.md` file] at the root of the "
"repository."
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"If you are using Quarkus and would like to be interviewed on our blog or "
"simply added to this file, please contact us and we will be happy to oblige."
msgstr ""

